From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Settings top level in ten BlackBerry 10 rows

Sable 2.0: the Settings homepage becomes ten rows, after BlackBerry 10's
settings list, with Sable first and Help last:

* Networks and connections, Notifications and sound, Apps, Display and
  look, Keyboard and input, Security and privacy, Accounts, Storage and
  backup, Battery, System and about.

Six of them are new grouped rows. Each opens SableSettingsGroupFragment
on a page (res/xml/sable_group_*.xml) listing the entries the homepage
used to show, with their own controllers, so every entry keeps its
summary, its visibility rules and where it opens; letters find a row as
on the Sable page. Apps, Keyboard and input, Accounts and Battery stay
direct rows. Nothing is hidden and search is unchanged. Both the classic
and the expressive homepage layouts change the same way.
